  "d16: 🍽️ Kate lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
  "d16: 🍽️ Kate leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d17: 🍽️ Ethan taps the pantry's fullest jar. \"More than we can eat before it turns. Rendering fat instead — the lamps won't fill themselves.\"",
  "d17: 🍽️ Dorothy taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d18: 🍽️ Liam rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
  "d18: 🍽️ Dany carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d19: 🍽️ Kate surveys the stacked shelves and nods. \"The wild can rest. Splitting firewood instead — winter comes whether we like it or not.\"",
  "d19: 🍽️ Chris leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d20: 🍽️ Ursula leaves the foraging basket at the door. \"The pantry can't take more — sitting with the elders instead.\"",
  "d20: 🍽️ Ethan looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d21: 🍽️ Ursula rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
  "d21: 🍽️ Ethan leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
